# Line endings.
#
# Every text file is stored with LF in the repository and checked out with LF
# in the working tree, on every platform. This overrides each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting, so the working copy always matches what is committed
# and what CI sees.
#
# Without it, Windows clones get CRLF on disk while the repository holds LF.
# Prettier normalises to LF, so `prettier --check .` then fails on nearly every
# file locally while passing on the Linux CI runner — noise that hides the real
# formatting failures.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files are detected automatically by text=auto, but declaring the ones
# we actually have makes that explicit and immune to a bad heuristic.
*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
